window.MFMWikiSearchIndex = [{"page":"index.html","id":"overview","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲百科","heading":"遊戲百科","text":"MFM / OFFICIAL WIKI 遊戲百科 從原創實體桌遊，走進線上六角棋盤。認識棋子的連接、封閉與計分，讓每一次落子都有方向。 六角棋盤、連接棋子、封閉得分。"},"en":{"title":"Game encyclopedia","heading":"Game encyclopedia","text":"MFM / OFFICIAL WIKI Game encyclopedia An original tabletop game, now an online hex-board strategy game. Learn to connect tiles, close regions, and make every move count. Hex spaces, connected tiles, and closure scoring."}}},{"page":"index.html","id":"explore","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲百科","heading":"探索 MFM","text":"- 百科條目 探索 MFM - 遊戲規則 棋盤、棋子、合法落子、封閉判定、DEAD 區域與計分。 - 模式與競技 自訂房間、AI、Ranked、RTG、賽季制度、觀戰與重播。 - 開發歷史 從 2020 年 3D 列印實體桌遊，到即時線上多人對戰。 從青銅到大師 Bronze Silver Gold Platinum Diamond Master 查看階級與評分門檻 →"},"en":{"title":"Game encyclopedia","heading":"Explore MFM","text":"- DATABASE Explore MFM - Game rules The board, tiles, legal moves, closed regions, DEAD and scoring. - Modes & competition Custom rooms, AI, Ranked, RTG, seasons, spectating and replays. - Development history From the original 3D-printable board game to online multiplayer. From Bronze to Master Bronze Silver Gold Platinum Diamond Master See tiers & rating requirements →"}}},{"page":"index.html","id":"origin","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲百科","heading":"先有桌遊，才有線上版","text":"- 遊戲起源 先有桌遊，才有線上版 MFM 的棋盤、規則、棋子、計分及平衡設計源自開發者的實體桌遊。2020 年公開 3D 列印版本，數年後再透過 Codex 協助將既有設計轉為軟體。遊戲玩法與設計決策仍由原作者負責。 查看 2020 年實體版紀錄 2020 年的 Monster Fusion Masters V1 原創 3D 列印桌遊。"},"en":{"title":"Game encyclopedia","heading":"A board game came first","text":"- ORIGIN A board game came first MFM's board, rules, tiles, scoring and balance originated in the creator's physical tabletop game. The 3D-printable edition was published in 2020. Years later, Codex helped turn the existing design into software. Gameplay and design decisions remain with the original creator. See the original 2020 edition The original Monster Fusion Masters V1 3D-printed tabletop game (2020)."}}},{"page":"rules.html","id":"overview","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲規則","heading":"遊戲規則","text":"- GAME RULES 遊戲規則 《Monster Fusion Masters》是一款運用六角棋子拼接、封閉白色區域取得分數的回合制策略遊戲。以下整理線上版目前採用的基本規則。 版本參照：Competitive Rule / Rule 20200629；線上玩法核對日期：2026-10-16。 從白邊的連接，到封閉後變成玩家顏色。"},"en":{"title":"Game rules","heading":"Game rules","text":"- GAME RULES Game rules Monster Fusion Masters is a turn-based strategy game. Connect hexagonal tiles and close white regions to score. These are the basic rules currently used in the online edition. Reference: Competitive Rule / Rule 20200629 · Online rules checked: 2026-10-16. From matching white edges to a closed region in the player’s color."}}},{"page":"rules.html","id":"board","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲規則","heading":"棋盤","text":"- BOARD 棋盤 棋盤由 61 個六角格 構成，中心向外延伸四圈。每格最多放置一枚棋子，已佔用或超出棋盤的位置不可落子。 棋盤上的棋子會影響相鄰格的合法方向與連通狀態，因此落子不只是填空格，也會改變後續可行的組合。 完整 61 格棋盤：中心一格，向外四圈；座標協助辨認落子位置。"},"en":{"title":"Game rules","heading":"The hex board","text":"- BOARD The hex board The board contains 61 hexagonal spaces : a center surrounded by four rings. Each space holds at most one tile. You cannot place a tile outside the board or on an occupied space. Placed tiles affect the legal orientations and connections of neighboring spaces. Each move changes the combinations available for future turns. The 61-space board: one center and four surrounding rings. Coordinates identify each placement."}}},{"page":"rules.html","id":"tiles","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲規則","heading":"棋子與牌庫","text":"- TILES 棋子與牌庫 每枚棋子有六條邊，每條邊為白色或黑色。按照白邊數量，棋子分為 0 至 6 白邊 的七類；同一類仍可能有不同白邊排列及內部連通形態。 白邊數 每局牌庫數量 0 邊 2 1 邊 16–30 2 邊 8–15 3 邊 8–15 4 邊 4 5 邊 2 6 邊 2 牌庫組成： 1 白邊的棋子數量是 2 白邊／3 白邊各自數量的兩倍；這三類隨當局抽選數量變化。每位玩家手牌最多 5 枚。 0 白邊 每局 2 1 白邊 每局 16–30 2 白邊 每局 8–15 3 白邊 每局 8–15 4 白邊 每局 4 5 白邊 每局 2 6 白邊 每局 2 圖中呈現遊戲內牌庫的各種形態；棋子可以旋轉。圖樣數量不等於每局牌庫張數。"},"en":{"title":"Game rules","heading":"Tiles & the deck","text":"- TILES Tiles & the deck Each tile has six edges, each either white or black. There are seven categories, from 0 to 6 white edges . Tiles in the same category may have different edge arrangements and internal connections. White edges Tiles per round 0 2 1 16–30 2 8–15 3 8–15 4 4 5 2 6 2 Deck composition: The number of 1-white-edge tiles is twice the number of each of the 2-white-edge and 3-white-edge categories. These three counts vary with the deck selected for the round. Each player may hold at most 5 tiles. 0 white edges Per round: 2 1 white edge Per round: 16–30 2 white edges Per round: 8–15 3 white edges Per round: 8–15 4 white edges Per round: 4 5 white edges Per round: 2 6 white edges Per round: 2 These are the shapes shown in the in-game deck. Tiles can rotate; the number of illustrated shapes is not the number of tiles in a round."}}},{"page":"rules.html","id":"placement","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲規則","heading":"合法落子","text":"- PLACEMENT 合法落子 從手牌選擇一枚棋子，必要時將它旋轉至想要的方向。 選擇棋盤內尚未被占用的格子。 所有與既有棋子接觸的邊必須配對： 白邊接白邊、黑邊接黑邊 。 若任一接觸邊不符，該方向與位置不能落子，需重新選擇。 遊戲畫面可用落子預覽確認合法位置；手牌也可以重新排列，並不改變棋子的屬性。 實際落子示範 逐枚落子，讓相鄰白邊連成同一個區域。 - 連接白邊 - 完成封閉 - 延伸再封閉"},"en":{"title":"Game rules","heading":"Making a legal move","text":"- PLACEMENT Making a legal move Select a tile from your hand and rotate it to the desired orientation. Choose an empty space within the board. Every edge touching an existing tile must match: white to white, black to black . If any touching edge does not match, choose another orientation or space. Use the placement preview to check legal moves. You can also rearrange your hand without changing the tiles themselves. IN-GAME MOVES Place tiles one by one to connect matching white edges. - Connect white edges - Complete a closure - Extend, then close"}}},{"page":"rules.html","id":"connections","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲規則","heading":"白色連通、封閉與 DEAD","text":"- CONNECTIONS 白色連通、封閉與 DEAD 白色邊相接後，會依棋子本身的連通形態形成一個或多個白色區域。 不只是相鄰就會合併，還要看棋子內部的白邊是否相通。 連通：白邊已接在一起，仍有尚未封閉的出口。 封閉：所有出口封住，區域轉成玩家顏色並得分。 DEAD：白邊通向棋盤外緣，區域變灰；紅邊標示外緣出口。 當一個白色連通區域沒有任何未封閉的出口時，會形成可計分的封閉圖形。同一個已計分區域不會因重複判定而重複得分。 若白色連通區域朝棋盤外緣延伸，因出口已無棋盤空格可延續，遊戲會標示為 DEAD 。DEAD 與成功封閉不同，不能單純當作封閉得分。 相同白邊排列，也可能有不同連通方式 中央不連通：兩端白邊屬於不同區域。 中央連通：相同白邊排列可以連成同一區域。"},"en":{"title":"Game rules","heading":"Connections, closure & DEAD","text":"- CONNECTIONS Connections, closure & DEAD Matching white edges form one or more white regions according to the internal connections of each tile. Adjacent tiles do not necessarily join the same region: their white edges must also connect inside the tiles. Connected: the white edges join, but an exit is still open. Closed: all exits are sealed; the region takes the player’s color and scores. DEAD: a white edge reaches beyond the board. The region turns gray; the red edge marks the boundary exit. A white region with no open exits becomes a closed shape that can score. A region that has already scored cannot earn points again through repeated checks. A white region extending beyond the board boundary has no space to continue and is marked DEAD . This is different from successful closure and does not count as a closed scoring region. The same white edges can connect differently Disconnected center: the two white ends belong to separate regions. Connected center: the same edge arrangement can form one region."}}},{"page":"rules.html","id":"scoring","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲規則","heading":"封閉計分表","text":"- SCORING 封閉計分表 封閉區域的分數由該白色連通區域涵蓋的 不同棋子格數 決定。 編號標出不同棋子格；同一格在同一個連通區域中只算一次。以下皆為遊戲實際判定的封閉範例。 1 2 2 格 → 1 分 1 2 3 3 格 → 2 分 1 2 3 4 4 格 → 4 分 1 2 3 4 5 5 格 → 7 分 1 2 3 4 5 6 6 格 → 10 分 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 7 格 → 14 分 1 枚棋子不構成有效得分區域；更大的封閉圖形通常能取得更高分數，但也更需要保留安全的延伸方向。 展開計分速查表 封閉區域棋子數 得分 2 1 3 2 4 4 5 7 6 10 7 以上 棋子數 × 2"},"en":{"title":"Game rules","heading":"Closure scoring","text":"- SCORING Closure scoring A closed region's score depends on the number of distinct tile spaces covered by that white region. Numbers identify distinct tile spaces. A space is counted once within the same region. Each example is a closure evaluated by the game. 1 2 2 tiles → 1 points 1 2 3 3 tiles → 2 points 1 2 3 4 4 tiles → 4 points 1 2 3 4 5 5 tiles → 7 points 1 2 3 4 5 6 6 tiles → 10 points 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 7 tiles → 14 points A single tile does not form a valid scoring region. Larger closed shapes usually earn more points, but require more care to keep their extensions safe. Scoring quick reference Tiles in the closed region Points 2 1 3 2 4 4 5 7 6 10 7 or more Number of tiles × 2"}}},{"page":"rules.html","id":"turns","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊戲規則","heading":"回合、PASS 與對局","text":"- MATCH FLOW 回合、PASS 與對局 每局開始時各玩家取得起始手牌；輪到玩家時會依牌庫與手牌上限補牌。玩家可以落子，或在需要時選擇 PASS。 連續 PASS 達 3 次 ，會失去繼續參與該局的資格；已取得的本局分數仍保留。成功落子後，連續 PASS 計數會依遊戲流程重置。 一般對戰採 3 局 ；Ranked 積分對戰採 1 局 。對戰最終結果由實際局數及系統結算規則決定。 提醒： 不同模式可設定回合時間；逾時可能自動 PASS。正式對戰判定以當前線上遊戲為準。 繼續閱讀：模式與 Ranked 制度 → 回合操作區：旋轉、選擇手牌、PASS 與確認落子。 對局狀態會顯示目前局數與回合；一般對戰為三局。"},"en":{"title":"Game rules","heading":"Turns, passing & matches","text":"- MATCH FLOW Turns, passing & matches Each round starts with an initial hand. On a player's turn, tiles are drawn according to the available deck and hand limit. The player may place a tile or choose PASS. 3 consecutive passes eliminate the player from further participation in that round. Points already earned in the round are retained. A successful placement resets the consecutive-pass count according to the game flow. Regular matches use 3 rounds ; Ranked matches use 1 round . The final result follows the actual match format and settlement rules. Turn timers: Time limits depend on the mode. A timeout may trigger an automatic PASS. The current online game is the authority for official rulings. Continue: game modes & Ranked → Turn controls: rotate, select a tile, PASS and confirm placement. Match status shows the current round and turn. Regular matches use three rounds."}}},{"page":"modes.html","id":"overview","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"模式與競技","heading":"模式與競技","text":"- MODES & RANKED 模式與競技 你可以用房間與朋友對弈、練習 AI 戰術，或透過 Ranked 參與一局定勝負的積分對戰。 大廳房間列表：尋找房間、加入對局或進入觀戰。畫面為示範資料。"},"en":{"title":"Modes & competition","heading":"Modes & competition","text":"- MODES & RANKED Modes & competition Create a room to play with friends, practice against AI, or join Ranked for a single-round rated match. The lobby room list: find a room, join a match or spectate. Demonstration data shown."}}},{"page":"modes.html","id":"game-modes","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"模式與競技","heading":"主要遊戲模式","text":"GAME MODES / 遊玩方式 主要遊戲模式 - CUSTOM ROOM 自訂房間 建立房間、分享房間代碼與邀請連結，最多四位玩家同場對弈，另可安排觀戰。 - AI BATTLE AI 對戰 與電腦對手交手，練習白邊連通、封閉得分與風險判斷；遊戲提供不同 AI 選項。 - RANKED 積分對戰 進入配對系統，按勝負與對手評分計算 RTG 變動，並參與當季排行。 - KNOCKOUT 淘汰賽 依賽事籤表進行對局，逐輪晉級；與 Ranked 的評分配對屬於不同賽制。"},"en":{"title":"Modes & competition","heading":"Ways to play","text":"- GAME MODES Ways to play - CUSTOM ROOM Custom rooms Create a room and share its code or invitation link. Up to four players can play together, with additional seats for spectators. - AI BATTLE AI battles Practice white-edge connections, closing regions and assessing risk against computer opponents. The game offers different AI options. - RANKED Ranked matches Use matchmaking to compete for seasonal standings. RTG changes depend on results and your opponent's rating. - KNOCKOUT Knockout tournaments Follow a tournament bracket and advance round by round. This is a separate format from Ranked rating-based matchmaking."}}},{"page":"modes.html","id":"rounds","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"模式與競技","heading":"一局與三局的差異","text":"MATCH FORMAT / 局數 一局與三局的差異 類型 局數 說明 Ranked 1 局 當局結果直接決定該場對戰結果。 一般對戰／AI 對戰 3 局 依完整對戰的局數與累積結果結算。 淘汰賽 3 局 晉級規則另有平手處理機制。 一局制不代表使用不同的落子或封閉計分方式；差別在於對戰結果的判定時機。 對局中的 ROUND 顯示目前局數；圖例為一般三局制。"},"en":{"title":"Modes & competition","heading":"One round or three?","text":"- MATCH FORMAT One round or three? Mode Rounds Result Ranked 1 The round's result decides the match. Regular / AI 3 Settled using the complete match's rounds and accumulated results. Knockout 3 Advancement has additional tiebreaking rules. A single-round match uses the same placement and closure-scoring rules. The difference is when the match result is decided. ROUND shows the current round. This example is a regular three-round match."}}},{"page":"modes.html","id":"ranked","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"模式與競技","heading":"Ranked 與 RTG","text":"RATING / RTG Ranked 與 RTG Ranked 的評分使用 Elo 系統。新帳號起始評分為 1200 RTG ，前 10 場 屬於定位期，評分可能較明顯波動。之後仍會依雙方分數與比賽結果調整。 目前遊戲 CLASSIC 徽章組 Bronze < 1100 RTG 未完成定位期時暫歸此級 Silver 1100+ RTG 完成定位期 Gold 1200+ RTG 完成定位期 Platinum 1300+ RTG 完成定位期 Diamond 1450+ RTG 完成定位期 Master 1600+ RTG 至少 30 場已完成對戰 定位期 前 10 場的評分狀態，與六個正式階級分開呈現。 關於顯示： 定位期是評分狀態，不代表額外的正式段位。階級、徽章與賽季展示可能持續調整，請以遊戲內當季資訊為準。"},"en":{"title":"Modes & competition","heading":"Ranked & RTG","text":"- RATING Ranked & RTG Ranked uses an Elo rating system. A new account starts at 1200 RTG . The first 10 matches are a placement period, during which rating changes may be larger. Ratings continue to adjust afterward based on both players' ratings and match results. CURRENT IN-GAME CLASSIC SET Bronze < 1100 RTG Also used provisionally during placement Silver 1100+ RTG Placement complete Gold 1200+ RTG Placement complete Platinum 1300+ RTG Placement complete Diamond 1450+ RTG Placement complete Master 1600+ RTG At least 30 completed matches Placement A rating status for the first 10 matches, shown separately from the six official tiers. Placement status: Placement is a rating status, not an extra official tier. Tiers, badges and seasonal displays may change; refer to the current in-game season information."}}},{"page":"modes.html","id":"features","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"模式與競技","heading":"輔助功能","text":"TOOLS / OTHER FEATURES 輔助功能 新手教學： 引導初次遊玩的玩家了解棋盤與對戰流程。 觀戰： 不進入玩家席也能觀看進行中的房間對局。 重播： 觀看與回顧已保存的對局。 色彩實驗室： 調整個人棋子顏色、圖案與視覺樣式。 玩家歷史與徽章： 在玩家資料中查看賽季及活動相關紀錄。 所有功能是否開放、可用數量與限制可能隨遊戲更新調整。 房間有獨立的 WATCH 觀戰席。 色彩實驗室：調整棋子的配色與圖案。 對局紀錄：依回合追蹤落子與得分。"},"en":{"title":"Modes & competition","heading":"More ways to explore","text":"- TOOLS More ways to explore Tutorial: Learn the board and match flow with guided instructions. Spectating: Watch a room's ongoing match without taking a player seat. Replays: Watch and review saved matches. Color Lab: Customize your tile colors, patterns and visual styles. Player history & badges: View season and event records in player profiles. Availability, limits and supported features may change with game updates. Rooms have a separate WATCH spectator area. Color Lab: customize tile colors and patterns. Game log: follow placements and points by turn."}}},{"page":"modes.html","id":"next","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"模式與競技","heading":"進一步閱讀","text":"NEXT / 相關頁面 進一步閱讀 遊戲核心規則與封閉計分 → 立即進入 MFM 線上遊戲"},"en":{"title":"Modes & competition","heading":"Keep exploring","text":"- NEXT Keep exploring Core rules & closure scoring → Enter MFM Online"}}},{"page":"requirements.html","id":"overview","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊玩與系統需求","heading":"遊玩與系統需求","text":"PLAY / SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS 遊玩與系統需求 Monster Fusion Masters（MFM）是免費線上回合制策略棋盤遊戲，可透過現代瀏覽器或 Windows 的 MFM Desktop 遊玩。 以下是初步硬體相容性參考，不是正式驗證的最低配備。 實際效能取決於瀏覽器、硬體、解析度與畫面特效；不保證固定 FPS。"},"en":{"title":"Play & system requirements","heading":"Play & system requirements","text":"PLAY / SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS Play & system requirements Monster Fusion Masters (MFM) is a free online turn-based strategy board game, playable in modern browsers or with MFM Desktop on Windows. These are preliminary hardware compatibility references, not validated minimum requirements. Performance varies by device, browser, resolution and visual effects. A fixed FPS is not guaranteed."}}},{"page":"requirements.html","id":"hardware","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊玩與系統需求","heading":"配備參考","text":"01 / HARDWARE 配備參考 項目 基本配備參考 建議配備（預估） CPU Intel Core i7-3520M 等級（實測參考，非最低界限） Intel Core i5 第 8 代或同級 記憶體 8 GB（估算，尚未驗證） 16 GB 顯示晶片 Intel HD Graphics 4000 等級（實測參考） Intel UHD Graphics 630 等級或以上 解析度 1280 × 720（參考） 1920 × 1080 網路 穩定網際網路連線 穩定網際網路連線 基本配備參考表示有接近此級別的電腦曾成功執行遊戲， 不代表 8 GB RAM 或所有同級 CPU、GPU 已通過測試 ；建議配備也不保證能穩定達到 60 FPS。"},"en":{"title":"Play & system requirements","heading":"Hardware reference","text":"01 / HARDWARE Hardware reference Component Basic reference Suggested (estimated) CPU Intel Core i7-3520M class (observed, not a minimum threshold) 8th-generation Intel Core i5 or equivalent RAM 8 GB (estimate, unvalidated) 16 GB Graphics Intel HD Graphics 4000 class (observed reference) Intel UHD Graphics 630 class or better Display 1280 × 720 (reference) 1920 × 1080 Connection Stable internet connection Stable internet connection The basic reference means a device near this class has run the game, but it does not validate 8 GB RAM or every comparable CPU and GPU . Suggested hardware is also an estimate and does not guarantee a stable 60 FPS."}}},{"page":"requirements.html","id":"platforms","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊玩與系統需求","heading":"遊玩方式","text":"02 / PLAY OPTIONS 遊玩方式 BROWSER 瀏覽器版 建議使用更新版本的 Chrome、Edge 或 Firefox。各瀏覽器的 Canvas 2D、動畫與圖形合成效率可能不同。 線上遊玩 WINDOWS X64 MFM Desktop 適用 Windows 10／11 64 位元，透過 Microsoft Edge WebView2 執行。需要 WebView2 Evergreen Runtime；完整解壓縮後可直接執行，無須額外安裝 .NET。 下載桌面版 · WebView2 Runtime"},"en":{"title":"Play & system requirements","heading":"Ways to play","text":"02 / PLAY OPTIONS Ways to play BROWSER Browser version Use an updated Chrome, Edge or Firefox browser. Canvas 2D rendering, animations and compositing performance can vary between browsers. Play online WINDOWS X64 MFM Desktop For 64-bit Windows 10/11. Uses Microsoft Edge WebView2 and requires WebView2 Evergreen Runtime. Extract the full portable archive; no separate .NET installation is needed. Download desktop · WebView2 Runtime"}}},{"page":"requirements.html","id":"performance","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"遊玩與系統需求","heading":"實際效能參考","text":"03 / PERFORMANCE 實際效能參考 開發者的一台舊型筆電配備 Intel Core i7-3520M、Intel HD Graphics 4000、16 GB RAM，螢幕為 1366 × 768。使用 MFM Desktop（WebView2）時，一般畫面約 30 FPS ，大量特效時曾下降到約 16 FPS 。 這是單一設備與場景的觀察，不是性能保證，也沒有驗證 8 GB RAM 的配備。遊戲提供的 30／60／120 FPS 動畫選項只設定更新率上限，不代表硬體一定能達成對應幀率。 如果畫面不夠流暢，可先嘗試 30 FPS 動畫模式、降低解析度及減少背景程式；Firefox 若表現不佳，也可以試試 Chromium 系列瀏覽器或桌面版。"},"en":{"title":"Play & system requirements","heading":"Observed performance","text":"03 / PERFORMANCE Observed performance On one developer-tested older laptop with Intel Core i7-3520M, Intel HD Graphics 4000, 16 GB RAM and a 1366 × 768 display, MFM Desktop (WebView2) generally showed about 30 FPS , sometimes falling to around 16 FPS during heavy visual effects. This is an observation from one device and certain scenes, not a performance guarantee. The 8 GB RAM estimate has not been validated. The 30/60/120 FPS animation options set update-rate targets and do not guarantee those frame rates. If performance is poor, try the 30 FPS animation option, a lower resolution and fewer background applications. If Firefox runs poorly, try a Chromium-based browser or MFM Desktop."}}},{"page":"history.html","id":"overview","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"開發歷史","heading":"開發歷史","text":"- DEVELOPMENT HISTORY 開發歷史 Monster Fusion Masters 並非從線上遊戲開始。它先是一款原創實體策略桌遊，經過多年構想與停滯後，才逐步完成可在瀏覽器遊玩的數位版本。"},"en":{"title":"Development history","heading":"Development history","text":"- DEVELOPMENT HISTORY Development history Monster Fusion Masters began as an original physical strategy game. After years of ideas and delays, it gradually became a digital game playable in a browser."}}},{"page":"history.html","id":"timeline","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"開發歷史","heading":"從實體棋盤到線上對戰","text":"TIMELINE / 沿革 從實體棋盤到線上對戰 規則核心：61 格六角棋盤。此圖為目前數位版本。 數位化後加入即時多人房間與 AI 對戰。 2020 / PHYSICAL BOARD GAME 原創實體桌遊公開 開發者完成 Monster Fusion Masters 的棋盤、六角棋子、玩法、計分與平衡設計，並公開 Monster Fusion Masters V1 3D 列印版本 。 AFTER 2020 / DIGITAL IDEA 數位化構想與暫停 原作者希望將實體桌遊轉成電子與線上遊戲，但因遊戲程式、多玩家伺服器開發技術與成本門檻，曾嘗試尋求外部開發協助，計畫仍擱置多年。 PROJECT REVIVAL / AI-ASSISTED DEVELOPMENT 透過 Codex 重新啟動 隨著 AI 輔助程式開發工具成熟，開發者重新投入專案，利用 Codex 協助將既有遊戲設計實作成軟體、分析程式、除錯與逐步重構。 原始遊戲設計、規則及玩法不是 Codex 創造的。 BROWSER PROTOTYPE / DIGITAL GAME 第一個可玩的數位版本 實作了棋盤呈現、棋子旋轉與放置、回合、封閉計分、手牌及操作介面，讓原本需要實體棋盤的對局可以在電腦中進行。 ONLINE / MULTIPLAYER 即時線上多人遊戲 陸續加入帳號、房間、玩家狀態同步、觀戰等功能。正式線上服務採用 Cloudflare Workers 與 Durable Objects 架構；這些核心程式碼不在公開 Showcase 內。 COMPETITIVE / RANKED & AI AI 與競技化 加入電腦對手、Master AI、Ranked 評分配對、賽季排名、淘汰賽、重播及新手教學，讓單機原型逐步發展為持續營運的線上競技遊戲。 ONGOING / CONTINUED DEVELOPMENT 持續更新與平衡 持續改良規則呈現、操作介面、遊戲效能、AI 及多人連線品質。遊戲與玩法方向仍由原作者決定；Codex 是軟體開發的協作工具。"},"en":{"title":"Development history","heading":"From tabletop to online play","text":"- TIMELINE From tabletop to online play The rule foundation: a 61-space hex board, shown in the current digital version. Digital development added real-time rooms and AI opponents. 2020 / PHYSICAL BOARD GAME The original tabletop release The creator designed Monster Fusion Masters' board, hexagonal tiles, gameplay, scoring and balance, and published the Monster Fusion Masters V1 3D-printable edition . AFTER 2020 / DIGITAL IDEA A digital idea, put on hold The creator wanted to turn the tabletop game into a digital and online game. The technical and financial barriers of game programming and multiplayer servers led to attempts to seek outside development help, but the project remained on hold for years. PROJECT REVIVAL / AI-ASSISTED DEVELOPMENT Restarting with Codex As AI-assisted programming tools matured, the creator returned to the project. Codex helped implement the existing design, analyze code, debug and gradually refactor the software. The original game design, rules and gameplay were not created by Codex. BROWSER PROTOTYPE / DIGITAL GAME The first playable digital version The board display, tile rotation and placement, turns, closure scoring, hand and controls were implemented, making it possible to play on a computer without the physical board. ONLINE / MULTIPLAYER Real-time online multiplayer Accounts, rooms, synchronized player state and spectating were added over time. The production online service uses Cloudflare Workers and Durable Objects. These core implementations are not included in the public Showcase. COMPETITIVE / RANKED & AI AI and competitive play Computer opponents, Master AI, Ranked rating-based matchmaking, seasonal rankings, knockout tournaments, replays and a tutorial helped the standalone prototype grow into an ongoing online competitive game. ONGOING / CONTINUED DEVELOPMENT Continuing to improve Work continues on rule presentation, controls, performance, AI and multiplayer quality. The original creator continues to decide the game's design and direction. Codex is a collaborative software development tool."}}},{"page":"history.html","id":"design-rationale","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"開發歷史","heading":"61 格棋盤與棋子配置的設計理念","text":"ORIGINAL DESIGN / 原始設計理念 61 格棋盤與棋子配置的設計理念 棋盤大小、棋子的種類與數量比例，以及封閉後的計分方式，是圍繞同一個目標設計的：讓玩家有足夠的時間與空間，嘗試拼出更大的怪物圖形。 BOARD SIZE / 61 CELLS 為什麼選擇 61 格？ 實體桌遊初期曾測試少一圈的 37 格棋盤，但實際對局很快就結束，棋子也容易碰到邊界，難以繼續向外延伸或拼出大型圖形。 改採 61 格，是希望讓單局時間維持在約十幾分鐘，同時保留足夠的拼接空間，在遊戲節奏與大型圖形的發展可能性之間取得平衡。 TILES & SCORING / 棋子與計分 為什麼這樣分配棋子？ 不同白邊數的棋子並非平均分配；棋子數量比例與封閉計分規則是一起考量的，目的是鼓勵玩家發展大型圖形，而不只是頻繁完成小型封閉。 計分方式刻意讓大型封閉圖形比拆成多個小圖形有更高的得分效率；但延後封閉也意味著要承擔對手干擾、空間受限或無法完成圖形的風險。 策略核心： 玩家要選擇立即完成小圖形、先取得分數，還是繼續延伸、追求更大的回報？61 格棋盤、棋子配置與計分方式共同創造了這種取捨。 目前採用的具體規則請參閱 棋子與牌庫 及 封閉計分 。"},"en":{"title":"Development history","heading":"Why 61 spaces and this tile distribution?","text":"ORIGINAL DESIGN / DESIGN RATIONALE Why 61 spaces and this tile distribution? The board size, distribution of tile types, and scoring for closed regions were designed around one goal: giving players enough time and space to build larger monster shapes. BOARD SIZE / 61 CELLS Why a 61-space board? Early tabletop tests used a board with one fewer ring, totaling 37 spaces. Matches ended too quickly, and tiles soon reached the boundary, leaving little room to extend connections into larger shapes. The 61-space board was chosen to aim for matches lasting roughly a dozen or more minutes, while leaving enough space for larger formations. It is a balance between match length and room for strategy. TILES & SCORING Why distribute the tiles this way? Tile types are not distributed equally. Their proportions were designed together with the closure-scoring system to encourage players to build larger regions rather than repeatedly close small ones. The scoring deliberately rewards larger closed regions more efficiently than splitting them into several smaller ones. Waiting to close a region, however, also risks opponent interference, running out of space, or failing to complete it. The strategic choice: Secure the points from a small region now, or keep extending it for a larger reward? The 61-space board, tile mix, and scoring system were designed to make that trade-off meaningful. See the current tile and deck rules and scoring rules for the exact gameplay details."}}},{"page":"history.html","id":"authorship","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"開發歷史","heading":"遊戲設計與程式協作","text":"CREATOR / DESIGN OWNERSHIP 遊戲設計與程式協作 Monster Fusion Masters 的核心概念、棋盤設計、棋子規則、計分方式和原始實體版本，均在現代 AI 輔助開發前完成。後續數位版本使用 Codex 參與規劃、實作、除錯與改善流程，但不改變遊戲原始設計的歸屬。 原創玩法核心：拼接棋子，封閉區域，依涵蓋格數計分。"},"en":{"title":"Development history","heading":"Game design & software collaboration","text":"- CREATOR Game design & software collaboration Monster Fusion Masters' core concept, board design, tile rules, scoring and original physical edition were completed before modern AI-assisted development. Codex later participated in planning, implementation, debugging and process improvements for the digital version. This does not change the authorship of the original game design. The original gameplay core: connect tiles, close regions and score by covered spaces."}}},{"page":"history.html","id":"sources","variants":{"zh-Hant":{"title":"開發歷史","heading":"資料來源與延伸閱讀","text":"REFERENCES / 公開資料 資料來源與延伸閱讀 Printables：2020 年 Monster Fusion Masters V1 實體桌遊 Showcase：繁體中文專案介紹與開發過程 Showcase：English overview MFM 線上遊戲 本頁為官方自述歷史，非獨立第三方報導；未經可核對來源證實的確切日期不另行臆測。"},"en":{"title":"Development history","heading":"Sources & further reading","text":"- REFERENCES Sources & further reading Printables: the 2020 Monster Fusion Masters V1 tabletop game Showcase: Traditional Chinese overview & development process Showcase: English overview MFM Online This is the creator's account of the game's history, not independent reporting. Exact dates are not invented where no verifiable source is available."}}}];
